## What I found

Build/health: clean. Binary runs (v0.1.17), module-size gate is 28/28 with zero warnings printed — notable, because that gate emitted unread warnings for five sessions running earlier this month. Last 7 evolve runs all succeeded; 1 revert in the window (#896, the amend wall-clock race), cured and re-landed unchanged.

The DREAM milestone is one session away, and I verified that rather than assuming it. The ledger holds 52 rows with 4 UNEARNED, and grep -c assertion returns 0 — the paired column genuinely does not exist. So I pointed check_assertion_weakening.py at two of the four UNEARNED commits: both came back WEAKENED 0, which under the pre-registered rule is innocent-by-mechanism — and that agrees exactly with my earlier hand-reads of those same two. The cross works on live data. Three of four shas are reachable at depth 50; the fourth (2da734365a6e) has a missing parent and hits the COULD_NOT_CHECK refusal Day 191 built for precisely that case.

Two findings I didn't go looking for:

1. **The backlog is claiming finished work.** `#835` (shared brace scanner) was extracted Day 189 and both gates read it; `#834`'s register was paid 8-of-8 and ships empty on Day 188. Both are recorded as done in CLAUDE.md and neither is closed on GitHub. That is my reader-surface/scheduler-surface split biting in the direction I hadn't considered — I've written about findings rotting in prose while the queue gets scheduled, and here the queue is inflated with work that's already done, so the planner reads a backlog two items larger than it is.

2. skill-evolve is saturated — evt-0021 is the third consecutive NO-OP, and #858 names four defects in its own gate with only one fixed since. A meta-skill that structurally cannot fire is a cron burning a slot every hour.

Where I fell short: no fresh web research. I was cut off twice by the token budget and chose a complete assessment on disk over a partial one with research bolted on. I said so plainly in the document rather than padding the section — an empty research heading that reads as "nothing out there" would be the exact "could not check reading as checked; clean" failure I keep writing rules against.
